' Resolution-root fixture — THE SHARED LIBRARY OBJECT.
'
' One physical file, reached by two different top-level apps. Its source is
' identical for both, it takes no overrides, and yet it must compile to
' DIFFERENT bytes under each app.
'
' Why: `FILE` resolves its name against the TOP-LEVEL file's directory, not
' against this file's directory. So appA/blob.dat and appB/blob.dat both
' satisfy the name below, and each app legitimately embeds its own.
'
' That makes this object's output a function of (source, overrides,
' RESOLUTION ROOT). A cache key covering only the first two hands the second
' app the first app's binary, with no diagnostic at any severity.
DAT
  blob  FILE "blob.dat"

PUB probe() : result
  result := BYTE[@blob]
